  "notes": "r3 investigator pass, owner-delegated verdict. Sparse two-skin LiDAR cloud (~0.25 pts/mm2 per skin; t 1.5 mm from skin pairs; outer bend radius ~2.2 mm so Ri ~0.8). Six real 90 deg formed folds, established from per-plane maps and perpendicular sections, none missed: F1 tall wall|strip, F2 strip|mid wall, F3 mid wall|base (4-segment stair, s 239.5..527), wall|tab (s 439.5..475.5), wall|end flange (two coplanar segments with a 10 mm relief gap) and wall|diagonal corner flange. A 12-14 mm window at s 364..378 interrupts all three long folds (strip cut out, mid wall lanced with a flat 10 mm tongue left in the base plane); a 62 mm base slot removes F3 at s 254..316, so B3 covers the main stretch 317..527. All extents are automatic, no extent override. fold_support_frac is informational here and near zero for every bend, including the ones verified in sections, because the cloud has ~1 point per mm per side within Ri+t+1 of a line. r3 prep: voxel 1.0, angle 20. Run margin 12 mm (wide support zone for the sparse cloud), small flanges 28 mm.",
